  data:  # 34b0
    kind: invariant  # 34b0
    title: "orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis stamps absolute path into Symbol.name and hardcodes span 1-1 (798 and 800 nodes affected); root cause of INV-dihif"  # 34b0
    status: violated  # 34b0
    priority: 2  # 34b0
    parent:  # 34b0
    tags:  # 34b0
    - analyzer  # 34b0
    - synthesis  # 34b0
    - path_handling  # 34b0
    - span  # 34b0
    - self_analysis  # 34b0
    - dogfooding  # 34b0
    isbefore:  # 34b0
    - INV-dihif-sufuv-kulik-hadiz-sokaz-fagus-najuk-jurub  # 34b0
    duplicate_of: []  # 34b0
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 34b0
    pr_ref:  # 34b0
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 14). Root cause for INV-dihif (filed round 10).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, the `orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis` producer creates file-kind Symbols with two correlated bugs:\n\n1. **798 of 809 file-kind Python Symbols have absolute paths in their `name` field** (while `path` is relative on the same node):\n   ```python\n   {\n     'id':     'python:packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_sketch.py:1-1:file:file',  # relative\n     'name':   '/home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_sketch.py',  # ABSOLUTE\n     'path':   'packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_sketch.py',  # relative\n     'origin': 'orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis',\n     ...\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **800 of 809 file-kind Python Symbols have `span={start_line:1, end_line:1}`** — hardcoded 1-1 instead of the actual file extent. A 3179-line cli.py is represented with span 1-1.\n\n**Root cause.** `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/analyze/base.py:375-385`:\n\n```python\nsynthesized[endpoint] = Symbol(\n    id=endpoint,\n    name=path,          # ← `path` is reconstructed from `endpoint` which has absolute form\n    kind=\"file\",\n    language=language,\n    path=path,          # ← same value but gets normalized downstream\n    span=Span(start_line=1, start_col=0, end_line=1, end_col=0),  # ← hardcoded 1-1\n    origin=\"orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis\",\n    origin_run_id=\"\",   # ← also empty, contributes to WI-higap\n)\n```\n\nTwo distinct values stamped into the Symbol then drift:\n- `name` and `path` start identical but `path` gets normalized (somewhere) to relative; `name` doesn't.\n- `span` is permanently 1-1.\n\n**This is the root cause of INV-dihif** (filed round 10). INV-dihif observed that `hypergumbo explain` leaks absolute paths in \"module level\" caller entries:\n\n> `- /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/.../test_sketch.py (packages/.../test_sketch.py:8)`\n\nMy round-10 hypothesis was that the explain formatter uses `Symbol.id` (which I expected to be absolute). Verified now: `Symbol.id` is RELATIVE for these nodes; the explain formatter is rendering `Symbol.name` which IS the absolute one. Fixing the name field here satisfies INV-dihif's symptom automatically.\n\n**Invariant statement.** No Symbol may have a `name` field containing an absolute filesystem path. The `name` field of a file-kind Symbol must be either the bare filename (e.g., `\"cli.py\"`) or the repo-relative path (matching `Symbol.path`). The `span` of a file-kind Symbol must reflect the actual file extent (start_line=1, end_line=<EOF>), not a hardcoded 1-1 sentinel.\n\n**Severity.** Medium. Concrete consumer impact:\n- 800 broken spans → any tool using `span.end_line - span.start_line` to measure file size returns 0 for every Python file.\n- 798 absolute-name leaks → INV-dihif's visible symptom + any other code path that renders `name` (search, sketch, etc.) potentially leaks.\n\n**Fix proposal.**\n\n1. **`name`**: derive the bare filename from `path`. `name = Path(path).name` (e.g., `\"cli.py\"`), or assign `name = path` after the relative-normalization step has run.\n\n2. **`span`**: when the orchestrator has access to the file (which it must, since the synthesizer is called after analysis), stat the file and set `end_line` to the actual line count. If line count is unavailable, set `end_line = -1` or `None` rather than `1` — a sentinel that consumers can detect, not a value that silently lies.\n\n3. **`origin_run_id`**: stamp the run signature (related to WI-higap, filed round 13).\n\n**Test gap.** Property test: assert no Symbol has `not Path(s.name).is_absolute()` AND `s.span.end_line >= s.span.start_line` AND `s.span.end_line > 1` for file-kind Symbols. Currently 798/800 violations on the self-analysis fixture.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/analyze/base.py:375-385` — the synthesizer (single fix point)\n- `INV-dihif-...` (filed round 10) — downstream symptom in explain output; will be satisfied by this fix\n- `WI-higap-...` (filed round 13) — empty `origin_run_id` (same producer; this finding includes that fix path)\n- `INV-ronuf-...` (filed round 6) — websocket linker creates phantom file Symbols; related to \"synthesizer creates problematic file Symbols\" pattern\n- `WI-fozoh-...` (done) — analyzer-side external_boundary file-kind duplication; this finding is about INTERNAL file-kind nodes, distinct scope"  # 34b0
    fields:  # 34b0
      statement: "No Symbol may have a 'name' field containing an absolute filesystem path. The 'name' field of a file-kind Symbol must be either the bare filename or the repo-relative path (matching Symbol.path). The 'span' of a file-kind Symbol must reflect the actual file extent, not a hardcoded 1-1 sentinel."  # 34b0
      root_cause: "analyze/base.py:375-385 (orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis) constructs file-kind Symbols with name=path where path is reconstructed from an absolute endpoint string, AND with span=Span(start_line=1, end_line=1) hardcoded. The path field later gets normalized to relative form downstream but name doesn't. The span never gets updated. Result: 798/809 file-kind Python Symbols have absolute names; 800/809 have 1-1 spans on self-analysis."  # 34b0
